'use strict';
/**
 * sweep_golden.js — characterization goldens for the TWO strategy enumerations.
 *
 * Why this file exists (P35 PR 1). The tool sweeps strategies in two places and they do not
 * sweep the same space:
 *
 *   - Monte Carlo's  buildVariations()      optimizer_core.js  — exported, reachable from node
 *   - The Optimizer's inline enumeration    optimizer_ui.js `_runOptimizerNow()` — NOT exported,
 *                                           not testable, unreachable from node
 *
 * They share `offGridParamFor` and `sameStrategySelection`, so the row IDENTITY cannot drift, but
 * the value lists can and already have: MC has no IRMAA-tier arm, no ACA arm, and caps IRA Draw at
 * 10% where the Optimizer runs to 20%. Nothing pinned any of that — the only assertions on
 * `buildVariations` were `length > 0`.
 *
 * P35 PR 2 extracts the Optimizer's enumeration into core as `buildStrategyFamilies()` so both
 * sweeps and any node harness can call it. An extraction can only be called behavior-preserving
 * against a recording made BEFORE it, which is what this file is. Everything here is a RECORDING
 * of what the code emitted, not a restatement of what it ought to emit; regenerate rather than
 * hand-edit (see "Regenerating" below).
 *
 * Loaded by `optimizer_core.tests.js` (node). Dual-mode export, the repo's classic-script contract.
 *
 * Regenerating
 *   MC half:  node sweep_golden.gen.js            (writes the MC_GOLDEN block below)
 *   OPT half: browser, see OPT_GOLDEN's own note — it needs a live `getInputs()` base.
 */

